Building WhyClick!! started from pure laziness: I just wanted to watch videos while eating snacks without getting grease all over my keyboard. I decided to make a touch-free media player using only basic browser code, but the journey was packed with funny mistakes. At first, the design was way too tall and messy, so I had to shrink the video screen and squeeze all the badges into a clean single line. Then came the voice control disasters. Whenever I said "louder," the code got confused and blasted the volume straight to a deafening 100%. To make matters worse, the microphone was so jumpy that a single word would trigger twice in a row, forcing me to slow it down with a cooldown timer and switch my keywords to "Fly" and "Down." I even broke the video uploader along the way and had to rebuild how the app loads video files.
